    rdfs:seeAlso <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo/RHEO_1000001>,
        <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo/RHEO_1000003> ;
    owl:inverseOf heo:hasRiskFactor ;
    skos:definition "Subject raises the probability of the outcome/disease Object."@en ;
    skos:example "Contraindication Risk factor for Adverse Event"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "A conceptual association, not an estimate of risk in any population. Read 'Heart Failure risk factor for Readmission' as a recognised association in the literature. It records that the literature treats the subject as a recognised risk factor for the object. Actual exposures, outcomes and estimated effects are described in RHEO."@en ;
    heo:applicationUse heo:FormalInference,
        heo:Navigation .

